## 0. Status, labels, conventions

**Status.** Proposed design text for independent review. Nothing has been implemented, executed, measured or accepted. A review PASS does not authorise implementation. Implementation and commit each need their own separate authorisation.

**Evidence labels**

| Label | Meaning |
|---|---|
| [M] | Measured earlier and reported to the author; not re-run |
| [R] | Reasoned |
| [P] | Proposed fixture, not executed |
| [U] | Unresolved; fails closed |

**Fixture status**

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **BINDING** | Expectation follows from binding decisions plus normative rules that do not depend on any open register item. Only these count as unconditional coverage. |
| **PENDING-OWNER(P-n)** | Depends on a PROPOSED item. The **interim** expectation, under that item's pre-decision behaviour, is given. If it differs, the **if-adopted** expectation is given too. |
| **PENDING-VERIFICATION(UR-n)** | Depends on unverified git or filesystem behaviour. |
| **GATED(G-F)** | Depends on the FETCH_HEAD positive-evidence gate (§1.6.6). The interim expectation assumes the gate is CLOSED. |
| **OUT-OF-MODEL** | A demonstration of a stated limitation, never counted as a correctness pass. |

**R6Δ** marks text that is new or changed relative to Revision 5.

**Register scope.** §2 lists policy choices only. Every PROPOSED item now has a **pre-decision behaviour (PDB)**: the normative, fail-closed behaviour the design uses until the owner decides (R5-07). Wherever a rule in §1 depends on a register item, it is tagged at the rule itself as `[P-n · PDB: …]`.

